NODE id=matrix/gateway/internal/rates.RateTableVersion kind=const
  digest=b3:70340c9bbe66f8529eb508ba50b636cadd63e5a93f2dc126949398060b9f74fd file=gateway/internal/rates/rates.go range=33:90 lang=go exported=true byte_range=1297:4825
  sig=untyped int
  doc=RateTableVersion identifies the immutable rate-card snapshot used to\nprice LLM calls. Bump on every schedule change. Ledger rows record\nthis so historical cost computations remain reproducible after a\nlater rate update.\n\nv2 (2026-06-01, v1 launch): added deepseek-v4-pro (planner upgrade +\ncompiler low-confidence escalation target) and kimi-k2.6 (executor\nupgrade). See FreeTierWhitelist + rateTable below.\n\nv3 (2026-06-04, PAX reference reprice): re-denominated the entire\nrate card from the placeholder 1 PAX = $0.01 anchor to the actual\nlaunch price 1 PAX = $11.43. No models added/removed and no USD\ntargets changed — every PAX-per-Mtoken value was recomputed as\nusd_per_mtoken / 11.43 (a uniform /1143 vs v2). Also introduced the\nDailyFreeTierLimitPax cap (10 PAX/day). Ledger rows priced under v2\nkeep their v2 figures; only v3+ rows use the new amounts.\n\nv4 (2026-06-08) adds glm-5p1-fast to the rate card for the new `neo`\nslot (Neo's cheap background model: write-back / compaction / summary\nvalidation). NOTE: the glm rate below is a PLACEHOLDER mirrored from the\ndeepseek-v4-flash tier — Andrew to replace with the real provider price.\n\nv5 (2026-06-10, Andrew approved) adds nomic-embed-text-v1.5 for the `neo`\nslot: Neo's cortex pager now does real semantic page-faulting through the\ngateway /v1/embeddings route. Embeddings are input-only (no completion\nside), so the output rate is 0. USD target $0.008/Mtoken (Fireworks list).\n\nv6 (2026-06-22, Andrew approved) adds deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro (Together)\nas Neo's main conversational loop model, replacing Qwen/Qwen3.7-Max on the\n`neo` slot whitelist. NOTE: the rate is a PLACEHOLDER mirrored from the\nFireworks v4-pro tier ($1/$2 per Mtoken) — replace with the real Together\nprovider price. The Qwen row stays on the card (still used by other slots).\n\nv7 (2026-07-01) ADDS the Baseten-served zai-org/GLM-5.2 (ModelGLM52) as the\nprimary chat model for every slot (Neo config + MCL DefaultRegistry now pin\nit; bare "<vendor>/<model>" now routes to Baseten in internal/routing). This\nis a purely ADDITIVE change: one new rateTable row + whitelisting GLM-5.2 on\nevery slot. All historical Fireworks/Together rows stay on the card so pre-v7\nledger rows remain replayable. GLM-5.2's PAX rate is a PLACEHOLDER pending the\nreal Baseten Model APIs price.\n\nv8 (2026-07-02, Andrew directed) REPLACES zai-org/GLM-5.2 with the\nBaseten-served zai-org/GLM-5.2 (ModelNemotron3Ultra)\nas the primary chat model on every slot (Neo config, Cody mode policy, MCL\nDefaultRegistry, deploy pins). One new rateTable row + the whitelist swap on\nevery lane. The GLM-5.2 row stays on the card so pre-v8 ledger rows remain\nreplayable. Nemotron's PAX rate is a PLACEHOLDER pending the real Baseten\nModel APIs price.\n\nv9 (2026-07-05, Andrew directed) MIGRATES the fleet off Z.ai GLM onto xAI\nGrok, REMOVING the zai-org/GLM-5.2 rows and ADDING three grok rows:\ngrok-4.3 (ModelGrok43 — Neo main + MCL triage/registry), grok-build-0.1\n(ModelGrokBuild — Cody), grok-4.20-0309-non-reasoning (ModelGrok420NR —\nCassandra + Neo cheap/consolidation + liaison). The Z.ai provider + upstream\npath are removed entirely; pre-v9 ledger rows that reference zai-org/GLM-5.2\nare NOT replayable against this card (accepted at migration). All three grok\nPAX rates are PLACEHOLDERS pending the real xAI prices.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/gateway/internal/rates/rates.go

NODE id=matrix/gateway/internal/rates.SubPax kind=func
  digest=b3:66a9bd4e1d1345cb5e2a48900d1910bbc5f16645742c35f642968887209430db file=gateway/internal/rates/rates.go range=419:442 lang=go exported=true byte_range=20746:21450
  sig=func SubPax(a, b string) (string, error)
  doc=SubPax returns max(a-b, 0) in PAX-denominated decimal-string form.\nUsed to compute X-Matrix-Daily-Remaining-Pax without re-querying.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/gateway/internal/rates/rates.go

NODE id=matrix/gateway/internal/rates.formatPax kind=func
  digest=b3:ab8d94a68af02e0adf8b22a4e38652eb4618947277ca21d65bb36015e203a8e3 file=gateway/internal/rates/rates.go range=485:490 lang=go exported=false byte_range=22853:23099
  sig=func formatPax(f *big.Float) string
  doc=formatPax stringifies a big.Float as a fixed-point decimal at 12\ndecimals (matching NUMERIC(20,12)). Trailing zeros are NOT trimmed\nso the wire format is stable across rows.
EDGES
  ^defines=matrix/gateway/internal/rates/rates.go

NODE id=matrix/gateway/internal/rates.rateIndex kind=var
  digest=b3:885b95f60792c8cf09aa899cb594260c0db31ad4367da0004e1ce7fd02fd3283 file=gateway/internal/rates/rates.go range=282:289 lang=go exported=false byte_range=14385:14604
  sig=map[string]rates.Rate
  doc=rateIndex maps model id -> Rate. Initialized once at package load.
